ã
ÇThis is a stonechat ‚Äî a wee, sturdy Scottish moorland bird whose call\nsounds like two stones clicked together, link by link. A hash chain\nwith wings.\n\n'raucle' is Scots ‚Äî Burns used it ‚Äî for rough, sturdy, fearless. A\n'raucle tongue' is blunt, honest speech: it tells you what actually\nhappened, not what you wanted to hear.\n\nThe bird is a raucle tongue with feathers. Small and unglamorous, it\nperches inside your agent stack, sees every tool call and every claim\nof authority, and speaks in signed receipts ‚Äî undiplomatic, unforgeable,\nand fearless out of all proportion to its size. A few kilobytes of\nEd25519 will happily contradict a billion-parameter model, because the\nmath defers to no one.\n\nIt saw what your agent did. It has the receipt.1341
ñ
çwarning: the 'raucle-detect' command is deprecated (the project was renamed); use 'raucle' ‚Äî this alias will be removed in a future release1342
